# 1 Expansion

$$ Z = ∫ Dψ Dψ̄ DA  e^{i S_0} e^{i S_int} = Z_0 ⟨ e^{i S_int} ⟩_0

$$ e^{i S_int} = 1 + i S_int + (i S_int)² / 2! + ⋯

Each S_int inserts one vertex e ψ̄γ^μψ A_μ at a spacetime point. n vertices come with 1/n!, which will cancel against the n! ways of assigning the n identical vertex factors to n points, exactly as in Lesson 49.

# 2 Contractions

The free expectation ⟨…⟩_0 is Gaussian. Wick's theorem pairs every ψ with a ψ̄ into S_F and every A with an A into D_μν. Unpaired fields at infinity, after Fourier transform and amputation, become the external spinors and polarizations of Lesson 51.

